ssessment"},{"text":"Adaptive learning"},{"text":"Educational content creation"},{"text":"Digital humanities"},{"text":"Language technology"},{"text":"NLP fundamentals"},{"text":"Translation technology"},{"text":"Multilingual content creation"},{"text":"Online teaching"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should be treated as a teaching and research support tool rather than a replacement for teachers. Teachers remain important for interpretation, mentorship, classroom relationships, critical thinking, and cultural context."},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 Outlook"},{"type":"p","text":"Language educators may increasingly work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI language tutors"},{"text":"Multilingual educational platforms"},{"text":"Speech-recognition systems"},{"text":"Automated language assessment"},{"text":"Personalised learning systems"},{"text":"Digital literary archives"},{"text":"AI-assisted translation"},{"text":"Virtual classrooms"},{"text":"Immersive literature experiences"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For regional languages, technology may also create opportunities for digital preservation, corpus development, NLP, speech technology, and global accessibility."},{"type":"h","text":"Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Language"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced grammar"},{"text":"Literature"},{"text":"Linguistics"},{"text":"Literary criticism"},{"text":"Communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Teaching"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pedagogy"},{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Classroom management"},{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Differentiated instruction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Literary analysis"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Publishing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LMS"},{"text":"Digital classrooms"},{"text":"Online assessment"},{"text":"Educational technology"},{"text":"AI-assisted teaching"}]},{"type"